-- 654_fall_halloween_pool_cleanup: the fall + Halloween holiday pools get the same audit the location and scenario
-- pools had (NIGHTLY_POOL_CLEANUP_PLAN.md phase 5; Kevin 2026-10-01: "can you run the same careful audit and repair on
-- the fall and halloween seed pools"). 7,714 live rows in 397 sub-themes across dual_scenarios, single_scenarios and
-- holiday_scenes.
--   1. Duplicates: scripts/clean-scenario-pools.js --holidays fall,halloween (one group read per sub-theme, then a
--      pair-by-pair confirm; 822 rows the confirm kept). 1,051 rows off; a 40-pair sample checked by hand, 40/40.
--   2. Fit: scripts/check-holiday-fit.js (first read + keep-by-default second read, then hand review). 3 off (winter
--      solstice snow / northern lights on Halloween), 2 reworded (candy-cane jars and a gingerbread house on Halloween
--      rows), 2 kept (a cider mill, a carriage of brooms).
--   3. Couple outfit lines that name a gown, dress, skirt, bodice or blouse without saying who wears it ("Both in
--      diaphanous white-grey gowns") put the man in it: the engine hands a couple row's attire over as "dress them in
--      this" and expects "She in ..., he in ...". scripts/fix-couple-attire.js read the 693 lines not in that form; 39
--      rewritten (36 from the read, 2 of those corrected by hand, 3 it missed), same costume, colours and props.
--   4. Goggles with no position (25 mad-scientist rows) can render over the eyes and stop the face swap: pushed up.
-- Every statement is guarded (still live / still the old text), so a re-run changes nothing. Rows are disabled, never
-- deleted. Thin sub-themes are refilled in 655.

-- 1. Duplicates (group read + pair-by-pair confirm): 1051 rows.

